{"id":"tuido-97259f","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md","action":"updated"},"created_at":"2026-10-02T13:13:19.862944Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.287 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"tuido-97259f","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-d9f3cadb-2db6-4ad7-935c-a3e8db1bcb02","text":"**Ready for review.** Not committed.\n\n**Changes**\n- `.github/workflows/ci.yml`: one Linux job runs on every push and PR to `main`: `fmt --check`, `clippy -D warnings`, then `test --locked`. A newer run on the same ref cancels the older one.\n- `.github/workflows/release.yml`: runs on `v*` tag pushes only.\n  - `verify-version` checks the tag against `Cargo.toml`.\n  - `build` covers 6 targets: Linux musl through `cross`, plus native builds for macOS and Windows. Each produces a `.tar.gz`/`.zip` and a `.sha256`.\n  - `publish` creates the GitHub Release.\n- `rustfmt.toml` sets `max_width = 120`. The one-time reformat touched `app`, `format`, `schedule`, `storage` and `ui`. Formatting only, no logic changes.\n- README: CI badge, an \"Install from a release\" section with a platform table, and a \"Releasing\" section.\n\n**Revision applied at the user's request (the spec was updated first):** removed the macOS/Windows CI test job and `workflow_dispatch`. Release binaries now build only on tag pushes, and regular pushes use Linux minutes only.\n\n**Decisions not in the original spec**\n- `softprops/action-gh-release@v3`, not v2, because v3 is current. Also checkout v7, upload-artifact v7, download-artifact v8.\n- Matrix values reach shell scripts through `env` (`TARGET`, `USE_CROSS`) instead of inline `${{ }}`. This avoids expression injection and fixes a shellcheck warning.\n\n**Verification**\n- actionlint, including shellcheck: clean.\n- fmt, clippy and 24/24 tests pass locally.\n- I ran the real build and the packaging script for `aarch64-apple-darwin`. The archive holds `tuido`, `README.md` and `LICENSE`, and `shasum -c` passes.\n- **Not verified yet:** static linking of the Linux musl binaries (the local Docker check was declined), and the Windows and cross-arch builds. These acceptance criteria are covered by the first tag push."},"created_at":"2026-10-02T13:13:53.660588Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.287 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
