{"id":"tuido-ae3d6f","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-8021266d-4269-4bed-971c-7007028d8a14","text":"**Implemented and reviewed.**\n\n**Changes**\n- `ui.rs`: new `DisplayState` enum with `display_state()`, which applies the precedence Completed \u003e Suspended \u003e Overdue \u003e Scheduled \u003e Plain and reuses `Todo::is_overdue`. It has per-state methods `prefix`, `text_style`, `row_style`, `icon` and `info_color`. `todo_item` and `render_info` now use it.\n- Suspended todos render yellow italic, or black on yellow when selected, and show no icon.\n- The Info panel shows `Status: Suspended · due \u003ctime\u003e` when the todo has a due date.\n- New `list_title()`: counts actionable todos and appends ` · M suspended`.\n- `app.rs`: `toggle_suspended` does nothing on completed todos.\n- Tests: 7 new, 31 in total. They cover the precedence table, rendered-cell styles (selected and unselected) for every state, icons, title variants, the Info panel text, and the `s` no-op.\n\n**Regression check:** the style tests, minus the suspended rows, also pass against `main`'s old `ui.rs`, so plain, scheduled, overdue and completed todos look exactly as before.\n\n**Open questions:** answered by the decision sub-agent and recorded in the spec. Follow-up `tuido-6e287f` was filed for a hide-suspended toggle.\n\n**Code review sub-agent:** APPROVE WITH NITS, all criteria met. All five findings are fixed:\n1. Strengthened the no-op test to cover a todo that is both completed and suspended.\n2. Exhaustive matches in `prefix` and `icon` instead of `_ =\u003e`.\n3. Reworded the guard comment.\n4. The due time is now formatted only in the match arms that use it.\n5. The test helper uses `checked_sub` instead of a subtraction that could underflow."},"created_at":"2026-10-02T13:23:46.514885Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.287 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
