{"id":"tuido-229065","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md","action":"updated"},"created_at":"2026-10-02T13:31:10.500628Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.287 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"tuido-229065","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-c2e51258-8395-4168-a20b-ef77460f9a8f","text":"**Implemented and reviewed. Also fixes bug tuido-2170e7.**\n\n**Changes**\n- New `cli.rs`: hand-rolled parser for `-f/--file PATH`, `--file=PATH` (UTF-8 only), `-h/--help` and `-V/--version`. If the flag is repeated, the last one wins. A value starting with `-` is rejected.\n- `storage.rs`:\n  - `resolve_todos_path` with an injected `PathEnv`: flag \u003e `TUIDO_FILE` \u003e XDG (with the legacy fallback) \u003e `~/.config`.\n  - `validate_explicit_path`: makes the path absolute and requires its directory to exist.\n  - `save_target` follows symlinks, including dangling ones, and never creates a link target's directory.\n  - The temp file is `\u003cname\u003e.tmp`.\n- `main.rs`: help and version go to stdout with exit 0, parse errors exit 2, resolution and load errors exit 1, all before the TUI starts.\n- `format::display_path` abbreviates the home directory to `~`. The help popup shows `File:` first and wraps.\n- README: new Configuration section covering the resolution order, switching to XDG, synced folders and symlinks, and that concurrent writers overwrite each other.\n- Tests: 49 in total, up from 31. The resolver tests never touch the real environment.\n\n**Open questions:** decided by the decision sub-agent; see the spec.\n\n**Code review sub-agent:**\n- First pass was REQUEST CHANGES:\n  - A dangling symlink was still clobbered. Fixed, with a reproduction and unit tests.\n  - `--file=\u003cnon-UTF-8\u003e` was rejected. Resolved by amending the spec to UTF-8 only instead of adding `unsafe` code; the reviewer agreed.\n  - Three nits, all fixed.\n- Re-review: APPROVE WITH NITS. Remaining: chained dangling symlinks resolve only one hop, a known LOW limitation already in the spec.\n\n**End to end with a scratch HOME:** checked the exit codes, the legacy fallback (the legacy file is written and no XDG file is created), saving through a regular symlink and a dangling one, and a relative `TUIDO_FILE`."},"created_at":"2026-10-02T13:33:36.427834Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.287 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
