{"id":"tuido-2170e7","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-1ee0af7f-b305-498a-98c8-118a12f40015","text":"Fixed in tuido-229065 (merge f891728). `save_todos` now goes through `save_target()`:\n- An existing path is canonicalized, so the real file is replaced and the link is kept.\n- A dangling link is resolved one hop to its target, whose directory must already exist and is never created.\n- The temp file is `\u003cname\u003e.tmp`.\n\nCovered by Unix tests for a symlink, a relative dangling link, and a dangling link into a missing directory. Known limitation: chained dangling links resolve only one hop."},"created_at":"2026-10-02T13:33:44.473691Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.287 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
