{"id":"tuido-9cc989","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-0a7d10a7-aa6c-434c-9ea4-d2f507bf15bd","text":"**Constraint from tuido-839e8f (persisted notification state):** once absolute dates are supported, a user can enter a due date that has already passed, for example \"Mar 1\" in April. The notification rule (`needs_notification`: overdue and `notified_at` is None or earlier than `due_date`) would then fire on the next check, notifying about a date the user just typed.\n\n**Fix in this issue:** in the add, edit and reschedule paths in `app.rs`, when a newly entered due date is `\u003c= now`, also set `notified_at = Some(now)`. The Info panel already shows it as overdue."},"created_at":"2026-10-02T13:38:20.883436Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.287 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"tuido-f6a453","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Tests leave tuido-test-* directories behind in the system temp dir","description":"Found by the code review of tuido-839e8f. The `temp_file` helper in `src/storage.rs` tests creates `$TMPDIR/tuido-test-\u003cpid\u003e-\u003cname\u003e/` and never removes it. Every `cargo test` run leaves a few more directories behind; the reviewer counted 61. Names include the process id, so runs don't collide. This is clutter, not flakiness.\n\n**Proposal:** add `tempfile` as a **dev-dependency** only, so there is no runtime or binary impact. Then replace `temp_file` with a `TempDir` that cleans up on drop, used by the storage tests and the notification restart test in `app.rs`. The alternative, a hand-rolled drop guard, is more code to maintain for no gain.\n\nLow priority: this is test hygiene only.","priority":4,"sort_order":"a6","dependencies":[{"source_id":"tuido-f6a453","target_id":"tuido-839e8f","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["task"]},"created_at":"2026-10-02T13:38:20.901993Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.287 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"tuido-839e8f","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-565c6f95-ead4-4a8b-baea-746b561d3ec4","text":"**Implemented and reviewed.**\n\n**Changes**\n- `model.rs`: new `notified_at` field (serde default, skipped when `None`) and `needs_notification()`: overdue, and `notified_at` is `None` or earlier than `due_date`.\n- `app.rs`:\n  - Removed the in-memory `notified` set and the `notify()` side effect.\n  - New `take_due_notifications(now)`: stamps each due todo, saves once, and returns the texts.\n- `format.rs`: `notification_message()` returns the single message unchanged, or a batched \"N todos overdue\" listing up to 3 texts plus \"…and K more\".\n- `main.rs`: `send_due_notifications()` runs on **every loop iteration**.\n- Tests: 55 in total, up from 49. They cover a model truth table, JSON compatibility, once per due date including later and earlier reschedules and the complete toggle, a restart round trip, message formatting, and loading an old-format file.\n\n**Decision sub-agent:** no re-arm when un-completing; no nag reminders; batch notifications; stamp at decision time.\n\n**Code review sub-agent:** APPROVE WITH NITS; all acceptance criteria met. Applied:\n1. Check on every loop iteration rather than only on idle ticks, so continuous typing can't delay a notification. The spec was updated first.\n2. Added a note on tuido-9cc989: stamp `notified_at` when the user enters a due date that has already passed.\n3. The restart test cleans up its temp directory. The same problem in the existing tests is filed as tuido-f6a453 (switch to `tempfile` as a dev-dependency).\n4. Added an app-level test for an earlier reschedule and a storage test that loads an old-format file through `load_todos`.\n\n**Cross-issue note** left on tuido-2203d3 (undo): keep the current `notified_at` when restoring from a snapshot.\n\n**Not run end to end with overdue todos,** because that would fire real desktop notifications. A smoke test with a scratch HOME confirmed the TUI runs and the file format is unchanged when nothing has been notified."},"created_at":"2026-10-02T13:39:12.967104Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.287 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
