{"id":"tuido-2203d3","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING","sort_order":"a1","dependencies":null,"labels":null},"created_at":"2026-10-02T13:41:44.959683Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.287 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"tuido-2203d3","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-0194a95b-1605-4fea-a06a-cb96cce19bee","text":"**Implemented and reviewed. Also fixes bug tuido-e97675.**\n\n**Changes**\n- `app.rs`:\n  - Snapshot-based `UndoEntry` with `undo_stack` and `redo_stack` (`VecDeque`, limit 100).\n  - `checkpoint(label, coalesce)` is called after guards and no-op checks.\n  - `restore(HistoryStep)` carries the current `notified_at` over by id and ends any run of merged moves.\n  - Merged moves keyed by todo id.\n  - No-op detection in `submit_input`: an edit is applied to a clone and compared as a whole.\n  - `Message { text, kind: Info | Error }`, with hints for destructive actions only.\n  - `u` (no modifiers) undoes and `Ctrl+R` redoes. Unbound Ctrl+letter combinations are ignored in normal mode, and `Ctrl+Y` no longer confirms clear-all.\n- `model.rs`: `Todo` derives `PartialEq` and `Debug`.\n- `ui.rs`: Info messages in cyan, errors in red; help text updated. README keybindings updated.\n- Tests: 68 in total, up from 55.\n\n**Decision sub-agent:** redo on `Ctrl+R`, 100 entries per session, keep the X confirmation, merge moves, hints only for destructive actions. It also found bug tuido-e97675.\n\n**Code review sub-agent:** APPROVE WITH NITS. Applied:\n1. **[should-fix]** `no_op_actions_record_nothing` cleared the stack before its only assertion, so it verified nothing. It now asserts after **each** case with a named message, and covers rescheduling to the same date and Ctrl+Y.\n2. The hint condition uses `!is_visible(index)`, so the future hide-suspended filter gets it for free.\n3. The edit no-op check compares whole todos (clone, apply, compare).\n4. `u` requires no modifiers; Ctrl+Y doesn't confirm clear-all.\n5. `HistoryStep` enum instead of a bool; the label is moved, not cloned.\n6. The UI colour test uses a distinctive marker.\n\nThe reviewer's grapheme-label nit needs no change.\n\n**Mutation-checked:** removing each of these makes a named test fail:\n- the `notified_at` carry-over\n- the \"undo ends a move run\" reset\n- the Ctrl guard\n- the redo clear\n- the reschedule and edit no-op checks\n- the suspend-on-completed guard\n- the Ctrl+Y guard\n\n**End to end in a pty with a scratch HOME:** add twice, `d`, `u`, `Ctrl+R`, `u`. The file contains both todos."},"created_at":"2026-10-02T13:49:12.321361Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.287 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
