{"id":"tuido-e97675","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-bc3d2cd0-40ab-4c0b-8c94-8aee55a8b2e6","text":"Fixed in tuido-2203d3. In `handle_normal_key`, `Ctrl+R` is matched first (redo), then any other `Char` with CONTROL is ignored, before the plain-letter arms. `u` now requires no modifiers, and the clear-all confirmation requires a plain `y`, so Ctrl+Y doesn't confirm. Covered by `unbound_ctrl_letters_do_nothing` (`Ctrl+D`, `Ctrl+S`, `Ctrl+X`, `Ctrl+J`, `Ctrl+U` do nothing, and `Ctrl+Q` doesn't quit) and by the Ctrl+Y case in `no_op_actions_record_nothing`. Both were mutation-checked."},"created_at":"2026-10-02T13:49:17.76333Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.287 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
