{"id":"tuido-9cc989","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-d2f8d088-73fc-4087-8573-38a7be8af1ff","text":"**Implemented and reviewed.**\n\n**Changes**\n- `schedule.rs` rewritten:\n  - A single `parse_due_date(text, now) -\u003e Option\u003cParsedDate { due, rest }\u003e` peels a **trailing run** of phrases off the end of the text.\n  - Phrase families: 12h and 24h times, `today`/`tonight`/`tomorrow`, full weekday names (with `on`/`by`/`next`), `in N minutes|hours|days|weeks` (and `a`/`an`), ISO dates, and month plus day (abbreviations allowed with a day number, ordinals, optional year).\n  - The families are listed in one `PARSERS` table.\n  - `clean_text` and `RE_CLEAN` are deleted.\n- `app.rs`:\n  - Add and edit use `rest` as the title.\n  - Reschedule must consume the whole input.\n  - Newly parsed dates in the past are stamped `notified_at`: after `checkpoint`, and for edits only after the no-op comparison.\n  - New `input_preview()` mirrors exactly what Enter accepts.\n  - A pending error clears on the next keystroke.\n- `format.rs`: `format_due_long` replaces `format_due_time`, which only the Info panel used, so this is a deliberate deviation from the spec. It's used in the Info panel and the input-title preview (`Add Todo → Fri 9:00am`).\n- README: phrase table, the trailing-run rule, and quirks. `demo/demo.gif` was re-recorded; a frame shows `Add Todo → Tomorrow 5:00pm`, and the recording finished before any seed came due.\n- Tests: 79 in total, up from 68. They include table-driven parse cases, false-positive guards and demo regression phrases.\n\n**Decision sub-agent:**\n- Trailing-run anchoring instead of an escape syntax.\n- Weekdays are always 1 to 7 days ahead.\n- Full weekday names only; month abbreviations only with a day number.\n- Past no-year dates roll to next year.\n- A long-format preview.\n- No `next week`-style phrases.\n\n**Code review sub-agent:** APPROVE WITH NITS. It checked about 45 probe inputs, including unicode, tabs, non-breaking spaces, overflow, and the America/New_York timezone; parsing takes about 1.2µs. Applied:\n1. **[should-fix]** The preview showed a date for date-only input, which Enter rejects (empty title). The preview now mirrors submit, with a test.\n2. Trailing punctuation (`Friday.`) and `3:16`-as-a-time are documented in the README and pinned by tests.\n3. Unknown relative units return `None` instead of defaulting to weeks.\n4. The parser table is a static slice, with a comment on how to extend it and why the order is safe.\n\n**Mutation-checked:** removing the end anchoring, accepting reschedule leftovers, skipping the stamp on add, letting a weekday mean today, or removing the year roll each makes a specific test fail."},"created_at":"2026-10-02T14:01:56.014006Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.287 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
