{"id":"tuido-f6a453","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-038e22e7-a96b-4baf-8e39-b4ecd06129ec","text":"**Implemented and reviewed.**\n\n**Changes**\n- `tempfile = \"3\"` added as a dev-dependency only. `cargo tree -e normal` has none. It resolves to 3.27.0, which requires Rust 1.63, below our MSRV.\n- New `storage::test_support::temp_todo_file() -\u003e (TempDir, PathBuf)` (`#[cfg(test)] pub(crate)`). It's used by every storage file test and by `app.rs::notification_state_survives_restart`. The old `temp_file()` and the manual `remove_dir_all` calls are gone.\n- `explicit_path_needs_an_existing_directory` now points at `dir/missing/todos.json`, so its \"parent doesn't exist\" assertion is as strong as before.\n- The fake-path tests (resolver `tuido-resolve`, `format::display_path`) are unchanged, because they never touch the disk.\n\n**Verified:** 278 `tuido-test-*` directories in `$TMPDIR` before and after three `cargo test` runs, so none leak now. 79/79 tests pass; clippy and fmt are clean.\n\n**No open questions:** the issue already chose the approach, so no decision sub-agent was needed.\n\n**Code review sub-agent:** APPROVE. It checked that every guard stays alive, that the symlink tests are safe on macOS (`/var` → `/private/var`), and the MSRV. One doc-comment nit, applied.\n\n**Not done here:** the 278 directories already left on this machine by earlier runs. That's a one-off cleanup, offered to the user."},"created_at":"2026-10-02T14:07:02.080165Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.287 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
